  {"date": "1995-10-11", "venue": "Compton Terrace Amphitheater", "city": "Chandler", "state": "AZ", "gap": 24, "set": "2", "out": ">", "nb": 1, "prev": "Mike's Song", "in": "->", "next": "Weekapaug Groove"},
  {"date": "1995-10-27", "venue": "Wing's Stadium", "city": "Kalamazoo", "state": "MI", "gap": 11, "set": "2", "out": ">", "nb": 1, "prev": "Simple", "in": ">", "next": "Keyboard Army"},
  {"date": "1995-12-11", "venue": "Cumberland County Civic Center", "city": "Portland", "state": "ME", "gap": 27, "set": "1", "nb": 1, "prev": "Tube", "next": "Julius"},
  {"date": "1995-12-29", "venue": "Worcester Centrum Centre", "city": "Worcester", "state": "MA", "gap": 7, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "-&gt; in from the historic &quot;Real Gin.&quot; &quot;McGrupp&quot; features an airy opening, replete with Trey's signature '95-style, Leslie-infused shimmering tone. Wonderful playing throughout. Page breaks for a dark calm, marked not so much by eeriness, but a general psychedelia, enhanced by an exotic, Eastern sentiment, combined with nice restraint by Trey. Great fills from Fish lead to a powerful conclusion.", "out": ">", "nb": 1, "prev": "Bathtub Gin", "in": "->", "next": "Big Black Furry Creature from Mars"},
  {"date": "1996-07-23", "venue": "Markthalle", "city": "Hamburg", "state": "Hamburg", "gap": 20, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "The jam section has a nice swinging vibe at first, with the others quietly supporting Page. Trey and Fish kick it up a few notches, then there's a sweet little salsa jam which sounds very much like &quot;The Landlady.&quot; This fun little jam seems to magically segue back into &quot;McGrupp&quot; proper and the customary closing section. Great version.", "nb": 1, "prev": "Down with Disease", "in": ">", "next": "Hello My Baby"},
  {"date": "1996-08-12", "venue": "Deer Creek Music Center", "city": "Noblesville", "state": "IN", "gap": 9, "set": "2", "out": ">", "nb": 1, "prev": "Prince Caspian", "in": ">", "next": "Run Like an Antelope"},
  {"date": "1996-10-26", "venue": "Charlotte Coliseum", "city": "Charlotte", "state": "NC", "gap": 13, "set": "2", "nb": 1, "prev": "Simple", "in": "->", "next": "Waste"},
  {"date": "1996-11-15", "venue": "Kiel Center", "city": "St. Louis", "state": "MO", "gap": 13, "set": "2", "out": ">", "nb": 1, "prev": "Maze", "next": "Split Open and Melt"},
  {"date": "1997-06-25", "venue": "L\u2019Aeronef", "city": "Lille", "state": "Hauts-de-France", "gap": 41, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "-&gt; in from &quot;Meatstick.&quot; A very unusual version. It starts in a swirly, funky mode, then shifts to a reggae style when the lyrics commence, and includes &quot;Makisupa&quot; teases. Trey narrates the lyrics in a style similar to the earliest versions (pre August '87). Page's solo is unusually quiet, but otherwise straightforward. A spacey ending transitions to &quot;Makisupa.&quot;", "out": ">", "nb": 1, "prev": "Meatstick", "in": "->", "next": "Makisupa Policeman"},
  {"date": "1997-07-31", "venue": "Shoreline Amphitheatre", "city": "Mountain View", "state": "CA", "gap": 18, "set": "2", "out": ">", "nb": 1, "prev": "Vultures", "next": "Mike's Song"},
  {"date": "1997-08-13", "venue": "Star Lake Amphitheatre", "city": "Burgettstown", "state": "PA", "gap": 8, "set": "2", "out": ">", "nb": 1, "prev": "Sleeping Monkey", "in": ">", "next": "Sample in a Jar"},
  {"date": "1997-11-26", "venue": "Hartford Civic Center", "city": "Hartford", "state": "CT", "gap": 12, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "An excellent version arriving midway through an excellent first set. Following a strong composed section, Page crafts an inspired passage, gently working a pleasant melody. Trey responds in kind, offering the perfect counter to Page's playing. While different from the typcially comedic &quot;Mule-Duel,&quot; the combination here jells, creating an inspired rise to the conclusion.", "nb": 1, "prev": "My Soul", "next": "Dirt"},
  {"date": "1997-12-30", "venue": "Madison Square Garden", "city": "New York", "state": "NY", "gap": 15, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "With Mike and Page out front early, Trey ultimately enters the fray, and he and Page break into an eerie, counterpoint-based duet of sorts, with Mike and Fish nearly absent from the mix. Mike and Fish finally jump back in, creating a tense, throbbing sentiment which gradually dissipates with no concluding section, and instead spills into an epic &quot;Harpua.&quot;", "nb": 1, "prev": "AC/DC Bag", "in": ">", "next": "Harpua"},
  {"date": "1998-04-05", "venue": "Providence Civic Center", "city": "Providence", "state": "RI", "gap": 5, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Great first-set placement affords room for dark, contemplative playing. Although Page dominates, full-band interplay takes hold, with Trey providing strong counterpoint to Page. Fish serves as the unsung hero, adeptly using the cymbals to keep a vibrant pulse, and adding tension as this swirling version builds to a cathartic conclusion.", "out": ">", "nb": 1, "prev": "Theme from the Bottom", "in": ">", "next": "Bathtub Gin"},
  {"date": "1998-07-05", "venue": "Lucerna Theatre", "city": "Prague", "state": "Prague", "gap": 5, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Despite a couple of rough spots spread throughout, the jam section features a contemplative, but at moments playful Page, with an intense culmination. An iconic '98-style, ambient Trey-led &quot;Jam&quot; follows &quot;McGrupp&quot; proper.", "out": ">", "nb": 1, "prev": "The Moma Dance", "in": ">", "next": "Jam"},
  {"date": "1998-07-19", "venue": "Shoreline Amphitheatre", "city": "Mountain View", "state": "CA", "gap": 8, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "With Fish nicely keeping time, Page embarks on a charged solo, playfully recreating Mike's bass line. Even with Page out in front, there is a growing sense that all are contributing to this classic '98 version. For the second consecutive time, an archetypal, ambient-style &quot;Jam&quot; emerges on the heels of a very fine &quot;McGrupp.&quot;", "out": ">", "nb": 1, "prev": "Jesus Just Left Chicago", "next": "Jam"},
  {"date": "1998-10-29", "venue": "Greek Theatre", "city": "Los Angeles", "state": "CA", "gap": 25, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Super, subtle, and very '98. Page drives a quiet jam featuring great Fish, and colored by Mike and Trey.", "out": ">", "nb": 1, "prev": "Birds of a Feather", "next": "Character Zero"},
  {"date": "1999-10-07", "venue": "Nassau Veterans Memorial Coliseum", "city": "Uniondale", "state": "NY", "gap": 70, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Trey gradually joins in with Page's serene and contemplative solo, offering his uniquely '99 tone in contrast to Page's classic piano musings. Sounding as though it may end in an uncharacteristically subdued manner, Page and Trey instead drive the playing out for another brief circuit, before closing in a more spirited and customary manner.", "nb": 1, "prev": "Mike's Song", "in": ">", "next": "Prince Caspian"},
  {"date": "2000-09-18", "venue": "Blossom Music Center", "city": "Cuyahoga Falls", "state": "OH", "gap": 60, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Trey deploys the Leslie, evoking shades of a '95 &quot;Slave,&quot; a bit of an anachronism pleasantly befitting '00. The jam provides a welcome cool down, featuring great and extended Page soloing augmented by Trey, who leads the band through an outro notable for an additional ambient pasage.", "nb": 1, "prev": "Twist", "next": "Halley's Comet"},
  {"date": "2003-07-29", "venue": "Post-Gazette Pavilion at Star Lake", "city": "Burgettstown", "state": "PA", "gap": 46, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "In the only version from 2.0, the others join in with Page for more of a rocking jam, with great Mike and Fish. There is also a sense of back and forth between Page and the others, giving the jam energy and a playful aspect as it builds to a solid conclusion.", "nb": 1, "prev": "When the Circus Comes", "in": ">", "next": "Golgi Apparatus"},
  {"date": "2009-06-16", "venue": "The Fox Theatre", "city": "St. Louis", "state": "MO", "gap": 44, "set": "e", "nb": 1, "prev": "The Star-Spangled Banner", "next": "While My Guitar Gently Weeps"},
  {"date": "2009-11-01", "venue": "Empire Polo Club", "city": "Indio", "state": "CA", "gap": 19, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Gorgeous acoustic version from Festival 8.", "note": "Acoustic.", "nb": 1, "prev": "Wilson", "in": ">", "xnext": "Driver"},
  {"date": "2010-07-03", "venue": "Verizon Wireless Amphitheatre at Encore Park", "city": "Alpharetta", "state": "GA", "gap": 34, "set": "1", "nb": 1, "prev": "Rift", "next": "Bathtub Gin"},
  {"date": "2010-10-20", "venue": "Utica Memorial Auditorium", "city": "Utica", "state": "NY", "gap": 20, "set": "1", "out": ">", "nb": 1, "prev": "Wilson", "in": ">", "next": "Saw It Again"},
  {"date": "2011-07-02", "venue": "Watkins Glen International", "city": "Watkins Glen", "state": "NY", "gap": 32, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Strong vocals and snappy playing by Mike in the composed section give way to a great Page-led jam. Backed by the band, and with some inspired contributions from Trey, a nice little &quot;McGrupp&quot; jam emerges, which rises and swirls into the customary closing.", "nb": 1, "prev": "Runaway Jim", "in": ">", "next": "Axilla"},
  {"date": "2012-06-28", "venue": "Klipsch Music Center", "city": "Noblesville", "state": "IN", "gap": 30, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "The rest of the band, particularly Trey, plays along during Page's solo, and there is some nice interplay between the two. Stepping into the lead, Trey migrates from the melodic to some mildly dissonant, atonal scales near the conclusion of this fine version.", "out": ">", "nb": 1, "prev": "Mike's Song", "in": ">", "next": "Back on the Train"},
  {"date": "2012-08-26", "venue": "Verizon Wireless Amphitheatre - Charlotte", "city": "Charlotte", "state": "NC", "gap": 16, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "A very strong composed section features great Trey. Then Page's forceful piano soloing is matched by a bit of full-band improvisation, with Trey coloring the jam with a few scattershot notes before settling into a nice, warm line. A really fun and inviting version.", "out": ">", "nb": 1, "prev": "Crosseyed and Painless", "in": ">", "next": "Mike's Song"},
  {"date": "2013-07-26", "venue": "Gorge Amphitheatre", "city": "George", "state": "WA", "gap": 24, "set": "1", "out": ">", "nb": 1, "prev": "Secret Smile", "next": "The Ballad of Curtis Loew"},
